abstract: >-
  Software and aggregate results for the JAMIA manuscript "Predicting 30-Day
  Hospital Readmission at Discharge: A Leakage-Safe, Calibrated Electronic
  Health Record Model in Medicare-Insured Adults". Versions v7 to v11 remove a
  prior-utilization feature (los_trend_180d) and two derived interactions
  that encoded later admissions; all earlier releases report inflated
  performance (see LEAKAGE_CORRECTION_v7.md). Contains the leakage-safe
  staged recursive feature elimination pipeline, the empirical
  first-admission leakage test, the final 48-feature XGBoost model
  (src/pipeline_v11), canonical machine-readable results
  (results_v11/final_model_v11.json and companions), and figures. Version v11 also rebuilt the feature table without global imputation. Out-of-fold
  AUROC of the complete selection procedure 0.7058 (95% CI 0.7017 to
  0.7104, primary); test AUROC 0.7060 (95% CI 0.6969 to 0.7151) on the
  historically exposed test partition, calibration slope 1.00. Same-cohort
  baselines: LACE 0.605 and HOSPITAL 0.649. MIMIC-IV row-level data are not
  included, per the PhysioNet Credentialed Health Data Use Agreement.
